			"notes": "## Authentication: operator reset + hardening\n\n### Operator account reset\n- **`/authreset <player>`** (op level 2) wipes a player's registration so they must register again — useful for forgotten passwords. Works on **offline players** too: the name is resolved via stored usernames, falling back to the deterministic offline-mode UUID. Online targets are kicked so they re-enter the normal join → lobby → register flow cleanly.\n- `UserData` now stores the player's username (backfilled on next login for existing accounts).\n\n### IP auto-login is now opt-in (default OFF)\n- New config **`enableIpAutoLogin`** (default `false`). IP-based auto-login is weak — it can be bypassed on shared NAT/VPN, and **behind a BungeeCord/Velocity proxy every player shares the proxy IP**, which would auto-authenticate everyone.\n- ⚠️ **Behavior change:** with this off, players must enter their password each session. Set `enableIpAutoLogin: true` in `config/combatpersistence.json` to restore the old convenience on trusted direct-connect servers.\n\n### Login brute-force protection\n- New config **`maxLoginAttempts`** (default 5) and **`loginLockoutSeconds`** (default 300). After too many wrong passwords the account is temporarily locked.\n\nBuilt for Minecraft 26.2 (Fabric).\n\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/PottersGame/combat-persistance/compare/v1.6.0...v1.7.0"
		},
